# The generated artifacts — five shell completions and eight man pages — are
# compared against what the clap model renders, and the renderer emits LF. A
# checkout that converts line endings (`core.autocrlf=true`, which the hosted
# Windows lane has) would put CRLF in the working tree: every artifact would
# differ from the model, and a shell completion carrying CRLF is a broken
# completion rather than a cosmetic one.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary files, so this only affects text.
* text=auto eol=lf
